# Repo-root `.env` — copy to `.env`. This is the only env file for local
# development; there is no `apps/web/.dev.vars`.
#
# Two consumers, one file:
#   1. process.env — drizzle-kit (packages/db/drizzle.config.ts) and the
#      cf CLI. Loaded by the `with-env` script (dotenv-cli).
#   2. The dev Worker's `env` binding — the dev server folds process.env into
#      the binding because `apps/web/cloudflare.config.ts` declares each secret
#      with `bindings.secret()`. Only names declared there reach the Worker, so
#      adding a new Worker secret means adding it in both places.
#
# In production the Worker names are set with `cf workers secrets update`.

# --- Cloudflare CLI (process.env only) ---
# `pnpm db:push` and `db:studio` target the local Miniflare D1 file and need no
# credentials. Prod D1 creds live only in `.env.production.local`.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=""
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=""

# --- Worker secrets (see `secrets` in apps/web/cloudflare.config.ts) ---

# Signs session cookies and the `/api/upload` / `/api/download` URLs.
# Any long random string: `openssl rand -base64 32`.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""

# Optional — enables `vg generate`. Leaving it empty logs a "missing required
# secrets" warning on dev boot and errors the media procedures at call time.
FAL_API_KEY=""

# Optional — TypeSafe System One judgments, including `vg playtest run`, the
# model-driven playtester: the server holds the key and proxies one decision per
# tick through `playtest.decide`; the CLI never sees it. Unset just means those
# calls error at call time; nothing fails at boot.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=""

# Optional — credit purchases through Stripe Checkout (`credits.checkout`, and
# the `/api/stripe/webhook` route that credits a paid session). Use test-mode
# keys locally; forward events with
# `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:5173/api/stripe/webhook`, which prints the
# whsec_ secret to use here. Unset just means checkout/webhook answer 412.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# The FAL_*_BASE_URL overrides in apps/web/env.d.ts are not secrets. To point
# at a fal mock, add them as text bindings in apps/web/cloudflare.config.ts.

# --- Production ---
# `.env.production.local` (gitignored) holds the prod Cloudflare
# account/database/D1 token and is read only by `pnpm db:push-remote`. Nothing
# loads it implicitly. Prod Worker secrets are in no file at all — they are set
# with `cf workers secrets update`.
